01:03:41.000 --> 01:04:23.000
pressure they were ever put under. Once Denise and Brian were married, he felt somewhat safe in the lie they were living, given they'd be protected by spousal privilege. That all changed when their relationship started to fall apart in 2012. Brian said they both became increasingly paranoid and would often pat one another down before they talked about anything serious in case the other was wearing a wire. They started to fear they were being watched. By the time Denise filed for divorce four years later, Brian was convinced she was going

96
01:04:23.000 --> 01:05:08.000
to talk. His paranoia at its peak, he broke into Denise's car in the early hours of August 5, 2016, and waited until she climbed behind the wheel. After making his confession, Brian led police down a remote, heavily vegetated stretch of road to an overgrown area off Carr Lake in the north of Leon County. The site had changed significantly since Brian last visited there, and he struggled to identify the exact location he was looking for. Pointing to one of the trees, Brian said,

